Add Texts 
Explore how to add text to images with OpenCV's putText function. Understand parameters like font type, size, color, and text position to customize image annotations effectively.

Let’s look at an example. We want to add the names of a company to all our images. We can use the OpenCV library to add text to all those images. Below are the steps we’ll follow in the lesson.



The lesson map
Add text
To add text, we use the cv2.putText() function of the OpenCV library. This function requires seven parameters, which are listed below:

img is the image to which we’ll add the text. text is the text we want to display in the image.
startingPoint is the starting pixel point of the texts.
cv2.FONT_HERSHEY_COMPLEX is the font type that we’ll display the text in. We can select other font types from the options in the OpenCV library.
fontSize is the font size.
blueColor adds blue color to the text. It can be changed to another color with a different color code. We’ll learn about this in detail in the next chapter.
thickness is the thickness of the text.

